text:
nora: Quick report from today's onboarding lab: our Go generator quickstart led a bunch of engineers to spawn background streaming goroutines tied to http.Request contexts. Under load we hit fd exhaustion and long-lived goroutines.

nora: Minimal bad pattern we saw in the sample app: 
```go
func handler(w http.ResponseWriter, r *http.Request) {
  go func() {
    ctx := r.Context()
    stream, _ := client.Generator.Stream(ctx, req)
    for stream.Next() {
      // write tokens to client, but client may disconnect
    }
    // missing Close()/drain, goroutine detaches
  }()
  w.WriteHeader(202)
}
```

lee: Classic. Two mistakes: detached goroutine + implicit trust that ctx cancellation cleans up network ops instantly. When auth rotation or transient retries happen the SDK's send loop can hold sockets open until retry succeeds, so leaked goroutines keep fds.

pat: Short-term fix: update quickstart and sample-app to demonstrate explicit lifecycle: create a child context, ensure stream.Close() in defer, and drain stream.Next() until false. Example we used in the workshop: 
```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(r.Context(), 15*time.Second)
defer cancel()
stream, err := client.Generator.Stream(ctx, req)
if err != nil { return }
defer stream.Close()
for stream.Next() { /* forward tokens */ }
```

nora: We pushed a small docs PR and updated the sample. Also added a short FAQ entry: "Why didn't my stream close?" with the pattern and note about auth-based retries.

lee: Medium-term ideas: add Stream.Done() chan struct{} and a CloseWithContext(ctx) method so callers can select{ case <-ctx.Done(): stream.CloseWithContext(ctx) } cleanly. Also emit a metric open_streams and add a debug finalizer that logs unreleased streams.

pat: For backwards compatibility add Done() and CloseWithContext() as additive methods and only change signatures in a v2. Also prototype a tiny go vet analyzer that flags patterns like `go func(){ ... r.Context() ... Stream(...) }()` and warn in workshops/CI.

devex-bot: Created issue devex/sdk-go#221 "stream ergonomics: Done/CloseWithContext + diagnostics" and sample-app PR #414 to update quickstart.

nora: Thanks — workshop attendees already noted less friction. We'll follow up on the SDK RFC and the vet rule. :thumbsup:
